# .agents/ Index

Deep reference for `<project-name>`. The root `AGENTS.md` states each rule in one line and links
here for the detail; this file is the table of contents an agent reads before opening any of them.

One row per file. The `Contents` cell says what a reader finds there and when it is worth the
tokens, in one sentence. A file that earns no row has no reason to exist here.

| File | Contents |
|------|----------|
| [<topic-1>.md](<topic-1>.md) | <What it covers, the rules it carries, and the evidence behind them> |
| [<topic-2>.md](<topic-2>.md) | <What it covers and the one decision it records> |
| [<topic-3>.md](<topic-3>.md) | <What it covers; name the gotcha it exists to prevent> |

Related, outside `.agents/`:

- `docs/<spec>.md` — <the spec this directory's files elaborate on>
- `.aidocs/conventions/` — <corpus or repo conventions that apply here>

Rules this index follows (from the docs convention):

- Every file under `.agents/` appears exactly once in the table above.
- The root `AGENTS.md` stays within its 20-80 line budget; anything past that moves here and
  gets a row.
- A row is a sentence, not a paragraph. Detail lives in the file the row points at.
- Paths are relative to this directory; no absolute paths, no links into another repo.
